    "body": "Heads up on the global BUN_OPTIONS install. With a space, `--preload /path`, every bun subcommand breaks: on bun 1.4.3 bun install, add, test, build and x all fail with `Script not found \"install\"` and so on. It's bun's parser, any value flag before the subcommand does it, e.g. `bun --define x:1 install`. `--preload=/path` works for both bun and Claude Code.\n\nI also gated install() on `Bun.main === \"/$bunfs/root/cli\"` plus execPath being a Claude Code install, so other compiled Bun binaries don't get their timers wrapped. Got the same 5/5/0 on 2.1.308 your way.\n"
  }
